# Zod Validation Patterns

## Schema Definition

Define schemas in `src/lib/schemas/` with type exports:

```typescript
import z from 'zod';

export const MySchema = z.object({
  id: z.string(),
  email: z.email(),
  createdAt: z.iso.datetime({ offset: true }),
  optionalField: z.string().optional()
});

export type MySchema = z.infer<typeof MySchema>;
```

## Validation Pattern

Always use `safeParse`, never `parse`:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD - safe parsing with error handling
const { success, data, error: err } = MySchema.safeParse(input);
if (!success) {
  // handle error
}
// use `data` (typed correctly)

// ❌ BAD - throws on invalid input
const data = MySchema.parse(input);
```

## Common Zod Types Used

```typescript
z.string()
z.email()
z.url()
z.iso.datetime({ offset: true })  // ISO datetime strings
z.enum(['value1', 'value2'])
z.object({})
z.array(z.string())
z.record(z.string(), MySchema)    // For key-value maps
z.custom<SomeType>()              // For external types
```

## Export from Barrel File

Add new schemas to `src/lib/schemas/index.ts`:

```typescript
export * from './myNewSchema';
```
